# Line endings
#
# Normalize every text file to LF in the repository and check it out as LF,
# regardless of each contributor's core.autocrlf setting. This matches the
# current working tree, so adding it causes no churn — and it stops the same
# file showing up as a whole-file diff just because it was touched on a
# different machine. Nothing here is a .bat/.cmd file, which is the usual
# reason to want CRLF on checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Source and config — stated explicitly so intent survives future edits.
*.py     text eol=lf
*.toml   text eol=lf
*.md     text eol=lf
*.cfg    text eol=lf

# Data. The Arabic corpora and datasets are UTF-8 text; keep git treating
# them as such so diffs stay readable rather than collapsing to "binary".
*.yaml   text eol=lf
*.yml    text eol=lf
*.json   text eol=lf
*.jsonl  text eol=lf
*.txt    text eol=lf
*.csv    text eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these. Trained models and the scanned/digital
# documents the pipeline ingests would be corrupted by EOL conversion.
*.joblib binary
*.pkl    binary
*.pdf    binary
*.docx   binary
*.xlsx   binary
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.tif    binary
*.tiff   binary
*.ttf    binary
*.woff2  binary
